Greeter accessibility with at-spi2: the greeter's gnome-session autostarts
at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop, which runs the at-spi 1.x (CORBA) registry
$libexecdir/at-spi-registryd. OpenIndiana has only at-spi2-core, so every
greeter start logs "Could not launch application
'at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop'" and the login screen has no assistive
technology support. With at-spi2 the session needs the AT-SPI D-Bus bus,
which then starts at-spi2-registryd on demand: run at-spi-bus-launcher
--launch-immediately, as at-spi2-core's own at-spi-dbus-bus.desktop does.
The file name and its translated names stay, so the package keeps its
paths. Later GDM releases dropped this entry altogether (at-spi2 is
started by the session); this is the 2.30 equivalent.

diff --git a/data/greeter-autostart/at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop.in.in b/data/greeter-autostart/at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop.in.in
--- a/data/greeter-autostart/at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop.in.in
+++ b/data/greeter-autostart/at-spi-registryd-wrapper.desktop.in.in
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 [Desktop Entry]
 Type=Application
 _Name=AT SPI Registry Wrapper
-Exec=@AT_SPI_REGISTRYD_DIR@/at-spi-registryd
+Exec=@AT_SPI_REGISTRYD_DIR@/at-spi-bus-launcher --launch-immediately
 OnlyShowIn=GNOME;
 AutostartCondition=GNOME /desktop/gnome/interface/accessibility
 X-GNOME-Autostart-Phase=Initialization
